================================================================================
Word frequencies — overview
================================================================================
CleverKeys' word lists come from three CC BY-SA sources, selected per list,
plus Leipzig Corpora Collection counts (CC BY 4.0) for Persian:

  List                                              Source
  ------------------------------------------------  -----------------------------
  bundled dictionaries (src/main/assets/            wordfreq (+ AOSP LatinIME
    dictionaries/) and langpack-<lang>.zip for        inclusion oracle where noted
    en, es, fr, de, it, nl, pt, sv, ru, el, tr, he,   below)
    uk, bg, mk, id, ms, tl; langpack-en-wordfreq.zip
  langpack-en-opensubtitles.zip,                    FrequencyWords (OpenSubtitles)
    langpack-en-opensubtitles-50k.zip
  langpack-sw.zip                                   Swwiki (Swahili Wikipedia)
  langpack-fa.zip                                   Leipzig Corpora Collection +
                                                      wordfreq (Lilak inclusion oracle)

Every list is modified: words were selected, filtered and ranked, and their
frequencies quantised into CleverKeys' binary dictionary format ("converted to
a CleverKeys frequency list"). Each langpack-*.zip carries its own NOTICE.txt
and "license" / "attribution" / "source" manifest keys, so the attribution
travels with a pack downloaded on its own (scripts/build_langpack.py;
docs/audit/2026-09-26-data-licensing-audit.md).

CC BY-SA 4.0 adaptations may be licensed under GPLv3
(https://creativecommons.org/compatible-licenses/; conditions at
https://wiki.creativecommons.org/wiki/ShareAlike_compatibility:_GPLv3 — keep
the attribution, licence notice and link, indicate changes). CleverKeys
distributes these adapted lists under GPL-3.0-only, with the attribution below.

================================================================================
Word frequencies — wordfreq
================================================================================
  wordfreq — Robyn Speer et al.
  https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq
  Code: Apache License 2.0 (no wordfreq code is distributed with CleverKeys)
  Data: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

wordfreq's frequency data combines, among others:

  * SUBTLEX word lists (SUBTLEX-US, SUBTLEX-UK, SUBTLEX-CH, SUBTLEX-DE,
    SUBTLEX-NL), created by Marc Brysbaert et al. and freely available at
    http://crr.ugent.be/programs-data/subtitle-frequencies. SUBTLEX is freely
    available data; its authors are credited here as its terms require.
  * OPUS OpenSubtitles 2018 (http://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles.php), whose data
    originates from OpenSubtitles.org (http://www.opensubtitles.org/) — see the
    OpenSubtitles section below.
  * Google Books Ngram Viewer data. Acknowledgement requested by Google:
    source Google Books Ngram Viewer, http://books.google.com/ngrams
  * Wikipedia (http://www.wikipedia.org), the Leeds Internet Corpus
    (University of Leeds Centre for Translation Studies) and ParaCrawl
    (https://paracrawl.eu), under Creative Commons licences.

