================================================================================
Shipped CTC script models — per-model provenance
================================================================================
CleverKeys ships one CTC swipe-emission encoder per script. Every one of them is
original CleverKeys work, trained from scratch, distributed under GPL-3.0 with
the app. This list is exhaustive; add a line here whenever a script model is
added.

Two delivery routes, both of them "shipped":

  * The Latin encoder is an APK asset (src/main/assets/models/).
  * Since 2026-09-10 the six per-script encoders travel INSIDE their language
    packs (scripts/dictionaries/langpack-<code>.zip, member model.onnx) rather
    than in the APK. Every one of those six languages needs its pack to decode
    at all, so the model reaches exactly the users who can use it — and nobody
    else carries 3.1 MB they cannot. The licence position is unchanged: the
    bytes are the same GPL-3.0 CleverKeys artifacts, distributed with the app's
    own language packs from the app's own repository.

  src/main/assets/models/ctc_swipe_encoder.onnx — Latin (en/fr/de/es/…).
    Trained on gesture data derived from the FUTO swipe corpus (MIT) and the
    How-We-Swipe shape-writing dataset (MIT); see the two sections above.

  langpack-ru.zip!model.onnx = ru_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Cyrillic (ru).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data: a learned trace generator fitted
    only to the same two MIT corpora above (FUTO + How-We-Swipe) emits Russian
    traces from a Russian word list and the on-screen layout geometry. No real
    Cyrillic gesture row appears anywhere in its pipeline — not in training, not
    in the validation split used for checkpoint selection. The Russian corpus
    used to *report* this model's accuracy (Yandex Cup 2023) carries no license
    grant, was therefore treated as research/held-out evaluation only, and
    contributed no bytes to any shipped artifact; the generator track that
    touched it is permanently unshippable. See
    docs/specs/ctc-architecture-and-multiscript-guide.md §3.3 and the licence
    seal note for the full record.

  langpack-el.zip!model.onnx = el_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Greek (el).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data from the same learned trace
    generator and MIT-only FUTO + How-We-Swipe source corpora described above,
    using a Greek word list and the shipped Greek layout geometry. No real Greek
    gesture row appears in training or checkpoint selection. Greek has no
    real-swipe evaluation corpus at any evidence tier; synthesis-holdout levels
    are not reported as accuracy.

  langpack-uk.zip!model.onnx = uk_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Cyrillic (uk).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data from the same learned trace
    generator and MIT-only FUTO + How-We-Swipe source corpora described above,
    using a Ukrainian word list and the shipped Ukrainian layout geometry. No
    real Ukrainian gesture row appears in training or checkpoint selection.
    Ukrainian has no real-swipe evaluation corpus at any evidence tier;
    synthesis-holdout levels are not reported as accuracy.

  langpack-bg.zip!model.onnx = bg_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Cyrillic (bg).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data from the same learned trace
    generator and MIT-only FUTO + How-We-Swipe source corpora described above,
    using a Bulgarian word list and the shipped Bulgarian layout geometry. No
    real Bulgarian gesture row appears in training or checkpoint selection.
    Bulgarian has no real-swipe evaluation corpus at any evidence tier;
    synthesis-holdout levels are not reported as accuracy.

  langpack-mk.zip!model.onnx = mk_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Cyrillic (mk).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data from the same learned trace
    generator and MIT-only FUTO + How-We-Swipe source corpora described above,
    using a Macedonian word list and the shipped Macedonian layout geometry. No
    real Macedonian gesture row appears in training or checkpoint selection.
    Macedonian has no real-swipe evaluation corpus at any evidence tier;
    synthesis-holdout levels are not reported as accuracy.

  langpack-he.zip!model.onnx = he_synth_v3_ch80_fp16w.onnx — Hebrew (he).
    Trained on 100% SYNTHESIZED gesture data from the same learned trace
    generator and MIT-only FUTO + How-We-Swipe source corpora described above,
    using a Hebrew word list and the shipped Hebrew layout geometry. No real
    Hebrew gesture row appears in training or checkpoint selection. Hebrew has
    no real-swipe evaluation corpus at any evidence tier; synthesis-holdout
    levels are not reported as accuracy.

================================================================================
Static context language model — Leipzig Corpora Collection
================================================================================
The bundled context models (src/main/assets/lm/<lang>.cklm, built by
scripts/build_static_lm.py) are derived from word-pair counts over these
Leipzig Corpora Collection downloads (web and news text):

  English     (lm/en.cklm)  eng-com_web-public_2018_300K
  German      (lm/de.cklm)  deu-de_web_2021_300K
  French      (lm/fr.cklm)  fra-fr_web_2013_300K
  Italian     (lm/it.cklm)  ita-it_web-public_2019_300K
  Portuguese  (lm/pt.cklm)  por-pt_web_2015_300K (weight 0.5) +
                            por-br_newscrawl_2011_300K (weight 0.5)
  Swedish     (lm/sv.cklm)  swe_news_2023_300K

Only pruned, quantised word-pair statistics are distributed; no sentence text
is shipped.

  Leipzig Corpora Collection — Universität Leipzig
  https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/download
  Terms: https://wortschatz.uni-leipzig.de/en/usage
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)

  D. Goldhahn, T. Eckart & U. Quasthoff: Building Large Monolingual
  Dictionaries at the Leipzig Corpora Collection: From 100 to 200 Languages.
  In: Proceedings of the 8th International Language Resources and Evaluation
  Conference (LREC'12), 2012.

CC BY 4.0 is compatible with GPLv3 redistribution; attribution is preserved
here. Source hashes are pinned in scripts/data/PROVENANCE.md.

================================================================================
Static context language model — Tatoeba
================================================================================
The same models additionally count sentences in their language from the
Tatoeba collaborative sentence database, weighted against the Leipzig counts
(English 0.1, German 0.25, French 0.05, Italian 0.1, Swedish 2.0; the
Portuguese model counts no Tatoeba sentence; the per-snapshot weight and hash
are recorded in src/main/assets/lm/<lang>.json).

  Tatoeba — https://tatoeba.org
  License: Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 France (CC BY 2.0 FR)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/

The contributors whose sentences were counted are listed, per language, in
files generated with each model:

  scripts/data/tatoeba-contributors-en.txt
  scripts/data/tatoeba-contributors-de.txt
  scripts/data/tatoeba-contributors-fr.txt
  scripts/data/tatoeba-contributors-it.txt
  scripts/data/tatoeba-contributors-sv.txt

